o pick out.\n- **Trend:** The `vltx_iv_history` series has only three yearly points: 24% in 2024, 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026. IV has drifted up slightly, but it sits within a 3-point range.\n\nWhether to buy therefore depends on your view of the stock, not on the price of the options. I haven't compared IV with realized volatility, because I found no data for it.\n\nOne risk bears on that view. Utilities account for 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of utility orders and Norvane is 21%, so a few customers drive demand. Their 2027 capex plans are up 18% and 12% (doc `utility-capex-2027`). Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026 (doc `datacentre-demand`). Those demand points belong to the sibling nodes (n2, n3). If you add to the position, the concentration in two utilities matters more than the option pricing.","ttft_ms":2392,"type":"result","duration_ms":20492,"uuid":"ac8457a8-3b22-454b-9b4c-00581b638ef2","ttft_stream_ms":1494,"time_to_request_ms":542,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":53,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":43,"input_attachments":90,"input_hooks":21,"conversation_append":17,"transcript_persist":98,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":63,"init_frame_send":14,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":31,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":14,"request_announcements":37,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":9,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":6,"request_build":20},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":266,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":93,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":169,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":94,"process_rss_mib_result":187,"process_anon_mib_result":106,"process_peak_rss_mib":187,"process_cpu_ms_turn":518,"process_wall_ms_turn":20491,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":114,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1601,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":1